*BUSINESS INTEGRATION PARTNERS CONSULTING IBERIA, S.L. no comunicará sus datos a terceros salvo obligación legal. Así mismo, el periodo de conservación de su CV como máximo 1 año, en el que será destruido.*
*Igualmente puede ejercer sus derechos de acceso, rectificación, supresión, oposición, limitación al tratamiento, portabilidad, y a no ser objeto de decisiones individualizadas automatizadas o consultar información adicional sobre el tratamiento en el correo : dpo\-bipspain@bip\-group.com.*

**Overview**
 Groupe Dynamite Inc. (GDI) is a Montréal\-based, public company of integrated omni\-channel brands, designing and distributing accessible, trend\-forward fashion for women since 1975\.




 Our mission of "Empowering YOU to be YOU, one outfit at a time" is brought to life through the GARAGE and DYNAMITE banners and represents the consumer\-centric core of GDI's long\-standing success as a leading retailer in North America.




 Today, GDI operates nearly 300 stores across Canada and the United States, as well as shoppable brand experiences at Garageclothing.com and Dynamiteclothing.com.




**Job Summary**
 As a Data Analyst at GDI, you will support strategic decision\-making by designing and building analytics\-ready datasets and delivering valuable insights across the organization. This collaborative role requires strong technical skills in SQL, Python, data modelling, and data visualization, as well as a solution\-oriented mindset. You will work closely with data engineers, QA, and business analysts to help meet the analytical needs of cross\-functional business stakeholders. As a core member of the Analytics team, you will contribute to a data\-driven culture and build high\-quality dashboards and analyses that inform business strategy.




**Requirements**
* Build accurate, informative, and stable stakeholder\-facing dashboards and reports in Sigma with guidance from senior team members;
* Collaborate with data engineers to support scalable and reliable data pipelines;
* Assess requirements to complete assigned tasks and communicate expected timelines, raising any workload challenges to your manager in a timely manner;
* Conduct analyses related to sales performance by applying techniques such as trend analysis, anomaly detection, forecasting, customer segmentation, and multivariate analysis to uncover actionable insights;
* Multitask by supporting three departments at once (e.g., Digital Marketing, Finance, and Operations);
* Clearly communicate findings and insights to both technical and non\-technical audiences;
* Participate actively in team standups and collaborate with a multi\-disciplinary team to accomplish shared goals;
* Contribute ideas for improving tooling, automation, and self\-service analytics as you grow in the role;
* Follow best practices in data governance and analysis by using version control (GitHub) and securely accessing, storing, and handling data.


**Required Qualifications**
* 1–3 years of experience in analytics, data science, or a similar role;
* Degree in Computer science, mathematics, business, or a related field;
* Proficient SQL skills and experience with dbt, Snowflake, and BigQuery;
* Willingness to learn and engage in version control and peer reviews via GitHub;
* Familiarity with Python for statistical analysis, API usage, and data transformation;
* Experience with data visualization tools such as Sigma, Looker, Power BI, or Tableau;
* Strong analytical and problem\-solving skills, attention to detail, and curiosity;
* Ability to work independently and as part of a collaborative team;
* Strong communication skills and a desire to grow in presenting data to varied audiences.


 At GDI, You Will Be Part Of a Growing Organization That Understands The Importance Of Investing In People And Offers You




* A comprehensive compensation package that includes performance\-driven bonuses;
* A group retirement savings program with employer matching;
* Flexible group insurance with personalized coverage that meets your needs;
* An employee discount at Garage and Dynamite;
* Exclusive private sample sales;
* A flexible vacation policy;
* And more!


 GDI has been repeatedly voted one of Montréal’s Top Employers and one of Canada’s Top Employers for Young People.




**Our promise…**
 No day will be like the last—we aim to be better today than we were yesterday. We are committed to employment equity.




 Candidates that are retained will be called for an interview.
